Check _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW before dereferencing it.

get_property returns NULL both when XGetWindowProperty fails and when the
property is absent, and the next line dereferences it on every captured frame.
It survives only because the window manager sets the property. free(NULL)
further down is already safe, and for the Desktop capturable both branches do
the same XShmGetImage on the root, so falling to the else branch on NULL
captures the same picture. Upstream bug.

diff --git a/lib/linux/xcapture.c b/lib/linux/xcapture.c
index 743021e..125f1a7 100644
--- a/lib/linux/xcapture.c
+++ b/lib/linux/xcapture.c
@@ -167,7 +167,8 @@ void capture_screen(CaptureContext* ctx, struct Image* img, int capture_cursor,
 
 		active_window =
 			(Window*)get_property(ctx->cap.disp, root, XA_WINDOW, "_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW", &size, err);
-		if (!ctx->wayland && *active_window == ctx->cap.c.winfo.win && !is_offscreen)
+		if (!ctx->wayland && active_window && *active_window == ctx->cap.c.winfo.win &&
+			!is_offscreen)
 		{
 			// cap window within its root so menus are visible as strictly speaking menus do not
 			// belong to the window itself ...
